<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40040" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quassātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				shaking</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capitum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 17, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cymbalorum,</span>”
				<i>a striking together</i>, <i>beating</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 7, 237</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quassationes,</span>”
				<i>shakings of the body</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 7, 15, 9</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A disturbance</i>, <i>affliction</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cessavit quassatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 105, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
